 "notes": "Crabel defaults (mult 1.0, 2T stop, EOD exit) are profitable on MNQ in both periods (PF 1.19 MAIN / 1.32 PRIOR) but 40% of MAIN net is one day (2025-04-09) and per-micro intraday DD is $5k, so Lucid fails (pass 0.16). NR7 / inside-day setup filters are rejected: they lead PRIOR (PF 1.6-2.2 on 27-66 trades) and lose on MAIN at mult 1.5/2.0 (grid rank corr -0.68); setup=none is a 12/12 plateau on both periods and mult 1.5 is best on both. Identified flaw: the 0.6xATR stop cap never binds, so the stop is 2-3x stretch (~0.4-0.6 ATR). Capping at 0.25xATR (plateau 0.15-0.4 at mult 1.5) with rr 1.5 target gives MNQ MAIN PF 1.25 / 323 trades / Sharpe 1.36 / +7.8k per micro, PRIOR PF 1.39 / Sharpe 1.81 (Lucid recommended on PRIOR). Lucid MAIN at 5 micros: pass 0.375, P(first payout) 0.14, exp net +807 point estimate but bootstrap lower bound -98 (not recommended); monthly pass rate 0.0-0.83, not consistent. MES: MAIN PF 1.38 but PRIOR 0.88 (fails robustness); MGC dead on both. EOD variant (cap 0.25) has higher PF on MAIN (1.39) but worse Lucid shape (pos days 43%, exp net -32). No engine bugs found."
